§ `The steps a party must take within a time`

DECLARE `Party to the step` IS ONE OF
    `the party who must take the step`

-- The steps, each with the rule that imposes it.
DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `serve the statement of claim`                               -- r 14.02
    `serve the defence`                                          -- r 14.04
    `file the summons for approval of the compromise`            -- r 15.08(2)
    `make discovery of documents`                                -- r 29.03
    `serve the hospital and medical reports`                     -- rr 33.07(2), 33.08(3)
    `file and serve the amended originating process and statement of claim naming the proper defendant` -- r 85.03

-- What the Rules say follows a missed step (the BECAUSE of each breach).
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step`
GIVETH A STRING
`what follows a missed` `the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `serve the statement of claim` THEN "the statement of claim was not served within 30 days after the appearance (r 14.02); the proceeding may be dismissed for want of prosecution (r 24.01(a))"
    WHEN `serve the defence` THEN "the defence was not served within the time limited (r 14.04); the plaintiff may enter or apply for judgment in default of defence (r 21.02)"
    WHEN `file the summons for approval of the compromise` THEN "the summons for approval was not filed within 30 days after the compromise, payment or acceptance (r 15.08(2)); without the Court's approval the compromise is not valid (r 15.08(1))"
    WHEN `make discovery of documents` THEN "discovery was not made within 42 days (r 29.03); the other party may serve a default notice (r 29.12.1) and seek an order (r 29.11)"
    WHEN `serve the hospital and medical reports` THEN "the hospital and medical reports were not served in time (r 33.07(2) or 33.08(3)); evidence not disclosed by a served report needs leave or consent (r 33.12)"
    OTHERWISE "the amended originating process and statement of claim naming the proper defendant were not filed and served within 28 days after the nomination was served (r 85.03)"

GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the step` `Step`
`the duty to` `the step` `within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the party who must take the step`
    MUST EXACTLY `the step`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the party who must take the step` BECAUSE (`what follows a missed` `the step`)

-- What became of the step. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the step
-- was taken, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether taking it today
-- would still be in time (the shape of the Civil Procedure Act 2010 encoding's helper).
DECLARE `What became of my step` IS ONE OF
    `taken in time`
    `not taken in time`
    `still open`

GIVEN `the step`                    IS A `Step`
      `the day the time starts`     IS A DATE
      `the last day`                IS A DATE
      `the step has been taken`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was taken`        IS A DATE
      `today`                       IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of my step`
`what became of the step` `the step` `the day the time starts` `the last day` `the step has been taken` `the day it was taken` `today` MEANS
    IF `the step has been taken`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time taken`), (EVENT `the party who must take the step` `the step` `the time taken`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `taken in time`
         OTHERWISE `not taken in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the party who must take the step` `the step` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not taken in time`
    WHERE
        `the rule` MEANS `the duty to` `the step` `within` (`the days from` `the day the time starts` `to` `the last day`)
        `the time taken` MEANS `the days from` `the day the time starts` `to` `the day it was taken`
        `the time now` MEANS `the days from` `the day the time starts` `to` `today`
